{"author":{"id":"29588b87a98184856c6eb9104921c34cca98a9cb029a2ee86cc10622d693ba86"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794791545,"nonce":"2Cvgm74MH9YgWCVjX1Utrhcf8j0=","title":"cn::input cannot take a height: InputSize fixes it at 32, 40 or 48 px","message":"`blinc_cn::components::input` sets `.h(config.size.height(theme))` from `InputSize` (Small 32, Medium 40, Large 48, from spacing tokens) and has no `height()` on `InputBuilder`. A style with its own control height (macOS regular 22 px, Windows 32 px, large touch style 56 px) cannot use it.\n\n`blinc_layout::widgets::text_input::text_input` takes any height (`.h()`), text size, radius, border and colours, so we build on that and lose the cn label/description/error wrapper. Measured: controls of 22, 32, 44 and 56 px come out at exactly those heights.\n\nWanted: `InputBuilder::height(f32)` (and text size) that overrides the size's value.","files":null}]}